Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 00:49:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-99540 [AFC][ACS][6GHz] Fix bandwidth-aware AFC rule
 selection in ACS power parsing

Issue:
mxl_acs_is_freq_rule_present_parse_power() matched the first AFC
frequency rule whose range covered the requested channel, without
requiring rule_bw >= requested_bw. This caused ACS to assign the
power limit of a narrower (e.g., 20 MHz) rule to wider channels
(40/80/160 MHz), inconsistent with the driver's regulatory limit
and resulting in incorrect TX power for SP mode ACS selection.

Fix:
Update mxl_acs_is_freq_rule_present_parse_power() to mirror the
driver's BW-aware AFC rule selection: skip rules with rule_bw <
requested_bw, then among covering rules pick the narrowest one,
breaking ties by lower EIRP. This ensures ACS assigns the correct
per-bandwidth AFC power limit consistent with driver behavior.

FIXUP to WLANRTSYS-83162 Ported afcd and composite mode changes from legacy hostapd
